  "notes": "USAGE:\n{失念|しつねん} is a formal and somewhat humble way to say \"I forgot.\" It is most commonly used in business correspondence, emails, and formal spoken language. Using {失念|しつねん} instead of {忘|わす}れる shows self-awareness and politeness when admitting a mistake.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is a formal word. In casual conversation, {忘|わす}れる is standard. {失念|しつねん} would sound stiff or overly formal among friends.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {忘|わす}れる: to forget (everyday word)\n- {度忘|どわす}れ: a momentary lapse of memory, tip-of-the-tongue forgetting",
